lers  so please proceed with caution you have  been  warned when we first meet hawks in the  boku no hero story  he is only 22 years old and he is  already the number three pro hero  hawks is the youngest hero to ever crack  the top 10 list  and after allmight retires hawks  advances to the number two pro hero  position  i have to admit that at first glance i  thought that hawks was just some cocky  entitled kid who was lucky enough to be  born with a great quirk  i guess that's just how his public  persona came off to me at first glance  however the more we learned about hawks  the more i realized that my initial  impression of him was completely  off in chapter 299 of the manga we  finally learned more about hawks's  tragic backstory  and this is definitely a rough one it  turns out that hawks's father  was a hitman for heyer who was on the  run from the law  he lived in squalor outside the city  with hawks and hawks's mother  a woman by the name of tomie hawks's  father was constantly paranoid that the  police were going to find him and arrest  him for murder  so he forbade hawks and his mother to  leave the house  he was afraid that if they ever left the  house they could end up attracting  attention  and the police would come and get him so  if  hawks ever left the house he would be  brutally punished  by his father hawks's father was abusive  towards his son and his wife  and he would straight up say to hawks  that he never should have been born  on top of that hawks's mother seems like  she might have had some mental or  developmental issues  and so she was never able to fully be  there for hawks or to support  him in any way hawks's childhood was so  rough that when he saw heroes on tv  he just assumed that they must be  fictional clearly they must have been  part of some tv show or movie because  stuff like that doesn't happen  in real life definitely not to him in  his own life  hawks suffered through poverty and abuse  every single day  and no hero ever came to rescue him from  his cruel life  but then one day hawks's father was  caught by the police apparently he tried  to steal a car  but then he was stopped by endeavour and  sent to prison  it was in this moment that hawks  realized that  heroes were real they were not just  fictional characters on tv  they really did exist and one of them  endeavor  just rescued hawks from his father's  abuse by throwing his father  in jail because of this hawks gained a  true sense of appreciation for heroes  and especially for endeavor but this was  not  the end of hawks's troubled childhood  his mother was afraid that she would  also be arrested for helping his father  hide from the police for all those years  so instead of going to the police and  telling them the truth she took hawks  and they went  into hiding yet again but because  hawks's mother didn't really have any  real world skills  hawks and his mom ended up homeless and  living on the street  hawks's mom was frustrated by the  situation and she asked hawks why he has  wings in the first place if he can't use  them to make their lives better  his mother's words made an impact on  hawks and he decided to start using his  quirk in a way that is useful to society  he started performing heroic deeds even  as a kid  and after saving a bunch of people from  a car accident the young hawks caught  the attention of the hero public safety  commission  the commission offered to keep hawks and  his mother safe and to take care of them  financially  if they agreed to abandon the takami  name and accept  new identities soon after the public  safety commission decided to train hawks  to become a special  type of hero so they separated him from  his mother and subjected him to intense  training for many years  which explains why hawks managed to  accomplish so much  at such a young age he was forced to  completely abandon his former life  and dedicate his entire existence to  special hero  training hawks would eventually open his 