 whom he considered his friend but  he also suffered severe  burn injuries at the hands of dobby  during that same tragic showdown  so although it's been clear for a while  that there is something shady going on  with the hero public safety commission  the true nature of their organization is  not revealed  until much later in the story when we  meet lady nagant  lady nagant was taken in by the public  safety commission when she was just a  child  much like hawks and she was lied to and  brainwashed until she became the  commission's  designated killing machine from groups  plotting alleged terrorist attacks  to hero groups who are believed to have  been associated with villains  countless civilians of the hero society  were secretly assassinated by the public  safety commission without  ever being given a right to a fair trial  and while the most famous and beloved  pro heroes  worked in the light and made the hero  society look virtuous  state-sanctioned assassins like lady  nagant were working in the shadows to  keep any potential enemies of the hero  society  under control by any means necessary  lady nagant  soaked her hands in blood over and over  again while obeying orders from the  public safety commission  while pretending to be a wholesome hero  in public she was secretly being told to  kill  again and again at one point the  chairman of the hero public safety  commission  ordered lady nagant to eliminate two pro  heroes who were allegedly provoking  fellow civilians into committing crimes  so that they would then capture them as  criminals and claim rewards  this is of course a serious accusation  but it is just an accusation and yet  without presenting evidence against  these two heroes during a fair trial the  chairman of the public safety commission  simply  ordered an assassin to kill them because  that was more convenient  when lady nagant pushed back against  this order  she was threatened by the chairman and  that is when she finally  snapped she killed the chairman and went  on to become a villain  rather than a hero and so when lady  nagant learns that hawks  is her successor within the hero public  safety commission  she assumes that hawks must be just as  demoralized and  jaded as she is lady nagant knows that  as her successor hawks must have been  forced to do all sorts of horrible  things  by the hero public safety commission and  yet  she is shocked to see that hawks still  has that heroic fire  in his eyes she doesn't understand how  this is possible  how can hawks maintain a heroic spirit  after all the darkness that he must have  been through  how can he still want to be a hero after  realizing that the people who were  running the entire hero society were  actually villains themselves  but hawks just smiles at lady nagant and  says that  at the end of the day he is an optimist  on top of that he had someone who  supported him  which is a reference to endeavour and  the inspiration that hawks drew from  endeavour  ever since he was still a child this  brief exchange between lady nagant and  hawks her successor  tells us everything we need to know  about hawks as a person  and as a hero despite his extremely  tragic childhood  despite the fact that he was used by the  hero public safety commission  and despite all the physical and  emotional scars that he has suffered  in the service of the commission hawks  refuses to give up on his dream  of being a true hero and saving innocent  people just like deku and meteo hawks  is an idealist at heart and he truly  believes that heroes can change the  world  for the better but at the same time  hawks has been through a lot and his  hands have definitely been stained with  blood hawks is not a fair weather hero  like those heroes who decided to retire  after things got tough and he is also  not the kind of hero who naively thinks  that he can save  everyone don't get me wrong hawks does  his best to save as many people as  possible  but he is also prepared t